Frankly, with fire resistance and a moderately good AC, you shouldn't
have died from fire ant bites.  You're looking at 2d4 damage per bite,
which should be mostly negated by your AC.  Any flammable objects
should, by this point, be kept in your BoH anyway.  That +2 GDSM is 11
points of AC, plus you should have 3 or 4 from your starting shield,
plus 1 or 2 from a helm, plus 1 or 2 from boots.  So at worst, that's a
-6, but really, a trip to minetown should put you around -10 or so.  At
that point, the ants won't be doing much.  But let's assume you were
really unlucky.  

If you had wands, you could have engraved.  Fire or lightning would have
been perfect, but digging probably could have saved you.  A /oTele isn't
going to work on you, but it works on the baddies.  Breaking it would
have sent them all away.  

